  "_method_foot": "R8.4a (2026-08-07). The R8.4 pass above read the HEAD band only -- printed page number, running head, sidehead, first lines. Masterplan 0.3 defines setting identity as 'same signature, same catchword, same line-end words', and the signature and catchword are both at the FOOT of the leaf, which a 16% head crop cannot contain. So R8.4 was STRONGER than 0.3 on page numbers (which 0.3 omits) and silently WEAKER on two of its three named criteria. The readings below close that gap on the constitution's own terms rather than amending the constitution to match the instrument. verify_setting.py now emits a FOOT band anchored on the text block, and these are read off it visually, not by OCR.",
  "_foot_limits": [
    "A signature appears only on the RECTO of the first leaves of a gathering, so a verso probe legitimately shows none. 'no signature in band' is therefore recorded as null, never as a disagreement.",
    "F's leaves carry the fatimamovement.com watermark and papal-keys device in the lower-left margin. The band's anchor samples right of centre (ANCHOR_X) to avoid it; the device still appears on the sheet and is not type.",
    "X is B upscaled (NCC 1.000 at +5), so X's agreement with B here is self-consistency, NOT independent corroboration -- exactly as for the head pass.",
    "OT-1635-M has no same-setting partner, so no foot pair exists for it. Its status is unchanged: sole witness, unverifiable, not verified."
  ],
